<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) (Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings)",
        "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) faithfully reproduces Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py> ;
    schema:about "Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: a quantitative match between the E5 simulation's P (1.22) and the specimen's P (1.07): chemistry and geometry differ, KS p < 0.01, reported as such",
        "does_not_claim: crystallographic (calcite / vaterite / aragonite) control of fibre texture",
        "does_not_claim: that uniform normal deposition alone explains the ooid: it rounds off faster than E3 predicts (minor-axis cortex 88 px vs major-axis 63 px)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Analogues: Carmel ooid asphericity 0.61 (nucleus) -> 0.29 (outer), 9 lamellae; Ag2CrO4 Liesegang rings P = 1.070 (CV 0.016), geometric r = 0.9972 / RMSE 2.37 px vs arithmetic r = 0.9880 / RMSE 4.66 px, gaps increase (Spearman 0.91, p = 7e-4)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E3 isotropic distance-transform front from a square nucleus: asphericity ∝ R^-0.97 (control: chessboard metric, exponent 0.00, square stays square)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E4 equal-rate Voronoi mosaic from hard-core (min separation 0.6 x mean spacing) centres, rendered with 8-px walls and measured by the same wall-segmentation pipeline as the plate: 6.10 neighbours, area CV 0.30 (Poisson centres: exact 5.78, area CV 0.56)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E5 radial Ostwald-supersaturation precipitation: 2-D b0 sweep 0.05/0.1/0.2/0.4 -> P = 1.290/1.220/1.170/1.130 (Matalon-Packter sign), 3-D a0 = 100: 7 bands; control without nucleation gap: 1 continuous deposit",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E6 dielectric-breakdown sweep eta = 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2: solidity 0.79 -> 0.17 (Pearson r = -0.92), mass-radius exponent 1.92 -> 1.18",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Plates: Fig. 196 outer-radius CV 0.0036, border radial-line index +0.57, 82 striae; Fig. 195 radial-line index +0.17 around 6 landmarked nuclei vs null +0.01 ± 0.06 (z = 7.1); Fig. 197 72 cells, 6.00 neighbours, area CV 0.28, KS p = 0.64 vs same-pipeline Voronoi; Fig. 208 lamella gaps ~24 px with within-ray CV 0.21, constant-gap fit beats geometric on 9/9 rays",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 421-422: Harting's CaCO3 precipitated in albumen forms 'large rounded concretions, with a more or less distinct central nucleus, and with a surrounding structure at once radiate and concentric'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 422: crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines'; p. 426: pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 424: with scanty albumin / scanty supply the globules become rough 'by an outgrowth of spinous or digitiform projections'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 427: Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre', offered as the cause of the concentric striation",
        "transfer_boundary: 2-D plate sections and 2-D lattice models stand for 3-D spherites; the synthetic spherite texture in the GIF is a drawing driven by the 3-D E5 band radii and the Fig. 196 striae count",
        "transfer_boundary: ooids and silver-chromate rings are modern analogues (labelled as such), not Harting's albumen spherites" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py; output: docs/media/t1917_023_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png; organism: Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 421-422: Harting's CaCO3 precipitated in albumen forms 'large rounded concretions, with a more or less distinct central nucleus, and with a surrounding structure at once radiate and concentric' | p. 422: crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines'; p. 426: pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles' | p. 424: with scanty albumin / scanty supply the globules become rough 'by an outgrowth of spinous or digitiform projections' | p. 427: Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre', offered as the cause of the concentric striation; reconstructed_in_script: E3 isotropic distance-transform front from a square nucleus: asphericity ∝ R^-0.97 (control: chessboard metric, exponent 0.00, square stays square) | E4 equal-rate Voronoi mosaic from hard-core (min separation 0.6 x mean spacing) centres, rendered with 8-px walls and measured by the same wall-segmentation pipeline as the plate: 6.10 neighbours, area CV 0.30 (Poisson centres: exact 5.78, area CV 0.56) | E5 radial Ostwald-supersaturation precipitation: 2-D b0 sweep 0.05/0.1/0.2/0.4 -> P = 1.290/1.220/1.170/1.130 (Matalon-Packter sign), 3-D a0 = 100: 7 bands; control without nucleation gap: 1 continuous deposit | E6 dielectric-breakdown sweep eta = 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2: solidity 0.79 -> 0.17 (Pearson r = -0.92), mass-radius exponent 1.92 -> 1.18 | Plates: Fig. 196 outer-radius CV 0.0036, border radial-line index +0.57, 82 striae; Fig. 195 radial-line index +0.17 around 6 landmarked nuclei vs null +0.01 ± 0.06 (z = 7.1); Fig. 197 72 cells, 6.00 neighbours, area CV 0.28, KS p = 0.64 vs same-pipeline Voronoi; Fig. 208 lamella gaps ~24 px with within-ray CV 0.21, constant-gap fit beats geometric on 9/9 rays | Analogues: Carmel ooid asphericity 0.61 (nucleus) -> 0.29 (outer), 9 lamellae; Ag2CrO4 Liesegang rings P = 1.070 (CV 0.016), geometric r = 0.9972 / RMSE 2.37 px vs arithmetic r = 0.9880 / RMSE 4.66 px, gaps increase (Spearman 0.91, p = 7e-4); transfer_boundary: 2-D plate sections and 2-D lattice models stand for 3-D spherites; the synthetic spherite texture in the GIF is a drawing driven by the 3-D E5 band radii and the Fig. 196 striae count | ooids and silver-chromate rings are modern analogues (labelled as such), not Harting's albumen spherites; does_not_claim: a quantitative match between the E5 simulation's P (1.22) and the specimen's P (1.07): chemistry and geometry differ, KS p < 0.01, reported as such | that uniform normal deposition alone explains the ooid: it rounds off faster than E3 predicts (minor-axis cortex 88 px vs major-axis 63 px) | crystallographic (calcite / vaterite / aragonite) control of fibre texture]; other sources: On Growth and Form (1st ed.), Ch. IX On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons, pp. 411-487 <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physa.2007.07.063>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-13>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-14>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-023-15>,
